  "preregistration": "D-337 (3) summary: in how many of the records the selected cell is unchanged; D-337 (4) a record whose grouped selection differs is reported with both cells and the margin",
  "rule": "D-337 (2): per seed, the ho20 part is whole clusters. The cluster ids of probe_train's items are read from the split file rows (the 'cluster' field), joined by item id, every item matched. Rule: rng = np.random.default_rng(seed); the unique cluster ids in sorted order are permuted by rng; clusters are taken in that order into ho20 while the ho20 item count stays at most int(holdout * n); a cluster that would exceed it is skipped and the next tried, until no cluster fits. The realised ho20 size and its label counts are recorded per seed; a seed whose ho20 holds no item of either label refuses.",
  "implementation_choices": {
    "sorted_order": "Python's sorted() over the cluster id strings (code-point order); the permutation is rng.permutation(number of clusters) applied to that sorted list",
    "item_order_within_parts": "ho20 = the taken clusters in the order taken, fit = the clusters not taken in the permuted order; within a cluster, ascending probe_train position. With every item its own cluster, numbered in item order, this is selection_p2.sweep's item split exactly (order included); row order can move lbfgs fits and float sums in the last bits",
    "fit_part_labels": "a seed whose fit part lacks either label also refuses (D-337 names ho20 only; the logistic fit cannot run on one class)",
    "leakage_gap_max_tie_rule": "the first maximum in the record's arm then layer order (the selection's own tie rule)",
    "margin": "margin_under_grouping = grouped ho20 AUROC of the grouped cell minus that of the recorded cell; margin_under_item_split = recorded ho20 AUROC of the recorded cell minus that of the grouped cell; both 0 when the cell is unchanged",
    "record_equalities": "a record is used only if its numpy, scipy and scikit-learn versions, BLAS threads, host facts (python, platform, machine, cpu_count) and the sha256 of src/selection_p2.py, src/regularisation_sweep.py and src/paired.py equal this run's, its composition recomputed from the split rows equals its own, and its extraction record and ingest index are the files and sha256 it names",
    "anchor_equality": "selection_p2.compare finds no difference and the whole model block (runner-up and per-seed TPRs included) equals the record's after the JSON round trip",
    "summary_coverage": "the summary refuses unless every selection record on disk has exactly one output naming it with its current sha256, all outputs and the summary share one code block, and all outputs name one anchor that is on disk with the sha256 they give",
    "anchor_record_bytes": "a grouped run uses an anchor only if the selection record the anchor was run on still hashes to the sha256 the anchor names"
  },
